E4 — merge_sorted(a, b) → list

Merge two already-sorted lists into one sorted list. Without calling sorted() or .sort().

([1,3,5], [2,4,6]) -> [1,2,3,4,5,6]
([1,2,3], [])      -> [1,2,3]
([], [])           -> []
([1,1], [1])       -> [1,1,1]

Variation of: two pointers. One index per list, take the smaller, advance that one. Then handle the leftovers when one list runs out — that's where this is usually failed. It's also the merge step of mergesort, so you can say that.

O(n + m) time. Say why it beats concatenating and sorting.